  "name": "gunship-3",
  "title": "Gunship 3",
  "description": "Gunship 3, among four rubble asteroids. Its engines burn lean: each exhaust parcel is four times heavier and leaves at about half the speed (100 m/s against 195), so each engine pushes about twice as hard (570 N): 12.8 m/s\u00b2 at full thrust, against Gunship 2's 7.2. Its welds are twice as strong. Its railgun launches 1 kg explosive shells at 96 m/s, the instant F is pressed (Gunship 2's gas cannon: 2 kg solid shells at 45 m/s), carries 40 and reloads in a quarter of a second. Its tractor's tether is 15 m. The exhaust no longer vanishes where the gas model lets it go: it carries on for a second as a tail that cools, spreads and fades, and still bounces off what it meets.",
